		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Computing union of overlapping pairs (simulation islands)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1864#p1864"><![CDATA[
I use the first algorithm in the link you provided:<br><br>------------------------<br>Off-line version:<br><br>    * Entire input is given at once.<br><br>    * Solution:<br>          o Scan input and place edges in undirected graph.<br>          o Run depth-first search to identify components and label each vertex.<br>          o Scan labels and print out classes (components). <br><br>    * Analysis: O(V + E).<br>      (Here, E = number of input pairs.) <br>----------------------------<br><br>To speed this up I maintain a connectivity graph at across time steps. This is exactly what ODE does (except it recreates the contact graph each step).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Fri Sep 22, 2006 5:37 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
